PLAIN-ENGLISH SUMMARY (not a substitute for the terms below)
================================================================================

You MAY, free of charge:
  • Use fx for any purpose, including commercial incident-response and
    forensic engagements you are paid for (e.g. a DFIR firm running fx on a
    client's evidence as part of a paid investigation).
  • Copy, modify, and build fx from source.
  • Share fx and your modifications, as long as this licence travels with it.
  • Use fx inside your own organisation without limit.

You MAY NOT, without a separate commercial agreement from the authors:
  • Sell, rent, sublicense, or otherwise charge a fee for fx itself or for a
    modified version of it.
  • Offer fx (or a derivative of it) to third parties as a paid product or as
    a hosted/managed/SaaS service whose primary value is fx's functionality.

In short: get paid for the investigative *work* you do with fx — don't sell
fx, or a repackaged/hosted fx, as the product.

The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind.

